## Q1 and Q2 findings

Q1 (runner tools): the four commands use bash, git, python3, node, and coreutils tools (grep, awk, sed, diff, cmp, mktemp, sort). No bun, jq, claude binary, or ra-quota appears in the four command trees. ubuntu-latest provides the listed tools, so no setup step is needed. Two dsh tests call `node --experimental-strip-types`, which needs Node 22.6 or later; the PR Actions run confirms the runner node version. No path or tool that cannot exist on a clean runner was found.

Q2 (paths outside the repo): no `/home/` path appears in any of the four command trees. The `/usr` matches are `/usr/bin/env` shebangs. The new workflow names no absolute path. The contract check `no-absolute-path` passes.

